---
import NewsletterBox from '../components/NewsletterBox.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Stuck in a Pickle" description="Why Stuck in a Pickle reads the long version so you can look at four drawings." canonicalPath="/about" image="/og.png">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="shell about-page">
    <header class="about-intro"><p class="label">About this operation</p><h1 class="headline">We read the long version so you can look at four drawings.</h1><p class="lead">Stuck in a Pickle is a comic publication about technology, politics, work, people, the internet, and other systems that are apparently functioning as intended.</p></header>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <aside><p>Our editorial policy, in full:</p><strong>Understand the news by making fun of it.</strong></aside>
      <section aria-labelledby="what-we-do"><h2 id="what-we-do">What we do</h2><p>Every Pickle starts with one short, factual sentence: what happened? Then comes a second question: what about this is quietly, structurally, magnificently ridiculous?</p><p>The comic takes that contradiction and removes everything except the part your brain will remember later while loading the dishwasher.</p><p>Every published story links to the reporting or primary source behind its factual premise. The dialogue and visual situations in the comics are satire; the underlying summary should remain traceable and accurate.</p></section>
    </div>
    <section class="sausage" aria-labelledby="sausage-title">
      <header><p class="label">A note on tools</p><h2 id="sausage-title">How the sausage is generated</h2><p>Metaphorical sausage. Literal pickles. Try to keep up.</p></header>
      <div class="roles"><div><h3>Computers may help</h3><ul><li>Discover stories worth examining</li><li>Summarize source reporting</li><li>Identify contradictions</li><li>Brainstorm joke premises</li><li>Storyboard comic beats</li><li>Assist with artwork</li></ul></div><div class="human"><h3>A human editor decides</h3><ul><li>What stories actually matter</li><li>Whether the summary is accurate</li><li>What is genuinely funny</li><li>What is mean, lazy, or misleading</li><li>What gets rejected</li><li>What earns a place in the jar</li></ul></div></div>
      <p class="bottom-line"><strong>The short version:</strong> tools can help make the thing. Responsibility does not get automated.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title"><h2 id="principles-title">House rules</h2><ol><li><span>01</span><strong>Clarity before cleverness.</strong><p>If the reader cannot tell what happened, the joke has no floor.</p></li><li><span>02</span><strong>Critique systems, not random civilians.</strong><p>Punching down is not satire. It is just falling over.</p></li><li><span>03</span><strong>Link the source.</strong><p>The joke may be ours. The fact should be traceable.</p></li><li><span>04</span><strong>Leave a human fingerprint.</strong><p>Personality is the whole point of a small weird corner of the internet.</p></li></ol></section>
    <NewsletterBox />
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem); }
  .about-intro { max-width: 59rem; }
  .about-intro .headline { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; }
  .lead { max-width: 49rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 2.2vw, 1.35rem); line-height: 1.52; }
  .about-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.75fr 1.25fr; gap: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 6rem); margin-block: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem); padding-block: 2rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--hair-strong); }
  .about-grid aside { align-self: start; padding-left: 1.25rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--pickle); font-family: var(--font-display); }
  .about-grid aside p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.85rem; font-style: italic; }
  .about-grid aside strong { display: block; margin-top: 0.55rem; font-variation-settings: "opsz" 40, "wght" 600, "SOFT" 26, "WONK" 1; font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.05rem); line-height: 1.12; }
  .about-grid h2, .sausage h2, .principles h2 { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-family: var(--font-display); font-variation-settings: "opsz" 72, "wght" 700, "SOFT" 32, "WONK" 1; font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 1.4rem + 2vw, 2.6rem); letter-spacing: -0.022em; line-height: 1.06; }
  .about-grid section p { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .about-grid section h2 + p { margin-top: 0.9rem; }
  .about-grid section p + p { margin-top: 0.9rem; }
  .sausage { padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); border-block: 1px solid var(--hair-strong); }
  .sausage header { max-width: 46rem; }
  .sausage header > p:last-child { margin-top: 0.6rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-family: var(--font-display); font-style: italic; }
  .roles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; margin-top: 2rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .roles > div { padding: 1.6rem 1.6rem 1.6rem 0; }
  .roles > div + div { padding-left: 1.6rem; border-left: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .roles .human { background: var(--brine); }
  .roles h3 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-variation-settings: "opsz" 40, "wght" 600, "SOFT" 26, "WONK" 0; font-size: 1.45rem; }
  .roles ul { margin: 1rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .roles li { margin: 0.4rem 0; }
  .bottom-line { max-width: 44rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 0; font-size: 1.02rem; }
  .principles { margin-block: 5rem; }
  .principles ol { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hair-strong); list-style: none; }
  .principles li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 0 1rem; padding: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .principles li:nth-child(odd) { border-right: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .principles span { grid-row: 1 / 3; color: var(--pickle); font-family: var(--font-display); font-variation-settings: "opsz" 30, "wght" 800, "SOFT" 22, "WONK" 0; font-size: 1.35rem; }
  .principles strong { font-family: var(--font-display); font-variation-settings: "opsz" 30, "wght" 600, "SOFT" 22, "WONK" 0; font-size: 1.22rem; }
  .principles p { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  @media (max-width: 46rem) { .about-grid, .roles { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .roles > div + div { padding-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); border-left: 0; } .principles ol { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .principles li { padding-inline: 0; } .principles li:nth-child(odd) { border-right: 0; } }
</style>
